menu "LakeShark"
    choice LS_BOARD
        prompt "LakeShark target board"
        default LS_BOARD_P4_NANO
        help
            Selects the board profile in components/lakeshark/board/.
            Everything the boards share (I2C, I2S, PA enable, uSD, the SDIO link
            to the on-board ESP32-C6) is identical across the Waveshare ESP32-P4
            family; this choice covers what actually differs - USB VBUS control,
            the display, and which header pins the Flipper link can use.

        config LS_BOARD_P4_NANO
            bool "Waveshare ESP32-P4-NANO (16MB)"

        config LS_BOARD_P4_WIFI6
            bool "Waveshare ESP32-P4-WIFI6 (32MB, no LCD)"

        config LS_BOARD_P4_TOUCH_LCD_4B
            bool "Waveshare ESP32-P4-WIFI6-Touch-LCD-4B / Smart 86 Box (32MB)"

        config LS_BOARD_P4_TOUCH_LCD_43
            bool "Waveshare ESP32-P4-WIFI6-Touch-LCD-4.3 (32MB)"

        config LS_BOARD_T_DISPLAY_P4
            bool "LilyGO T-Display-P4 (16MB)"
            help
                AMOLED display and peripherals defined by the T-Display-P4
                board profile in components/lakeshark/board/variants/.
    endchoice

    choice LS_TDP4_PANEL
        prompt "T-Display-P4 display SKU"
        depends on LS_BOARD_T_DISPLAY_P4
        default LS_TDP4_PANEL_RM69A10
        help
            The T-Display-P4 ships with one of two MIPI-DSI panels. They differ
            in resolution, timings, brightness control and touch controller,
            so the image must be built for the one fitted.

        config LS_TDP4_PANEL_RM69A10
            bool "4.1\" AMOLED, RM69A10 568x1232, GT9895 touch"

        config LS_TDP4_PANEL_HI8561
            bool "TFT, HI8561 540x1168, HI8561 touch, PT4103 backlight"
    endchoice

    config LS_LR2021_ONLY
        bool "LakeShark LR: LR2021 boards only, no USB dongles or SX1262"
        depends on LS_BOARD_T_DISPLAY_P4
        default n
        help
            Builds the LR edition for the T-Display-P4 LR2021 variant. Leaves
            out the USB host stack, the RTL-SDR and HackRF drivers, the SX1262
            driver and the apps that need a dongle (CELL, CATCH, ACARS), and
            spends the memory on the LR2021. The image refuses SX1262 boards.

    config LS_SD_MAX_FREQ_KHZ
        int "SD card maximum clock (kHz)"
        range 20000 40000
        default 40000 if LS_BOARD_T_DISPLAY_P4
        default 20000
        help
            T-Display-P4 supports 3.3 V high-speed SDR on slot 0. Mount
            initialization or verification failures retry at 20 MHz.
            Set 20000 to force the original clock. No UHS voltage switch.

    config LS_PANEL_RUNTIME
        bool "Waveshare DSI panel chosen at runtime ('panel' command)"
        depends on LS_BOARD_P4_NANO && LAKESHARK_HEADLESS
        default n
        help
            Builds in the TUI and a driver for Waveshare's MIPI-DSI panels on
            the board's DSI connector. Nothing changes until a panel is saved
            with 'panel set <name>'; with none the board stays headless.

    config LS_VBUS_EN_GPIO
        int "USB host VBUS enable GPIO (-1 if the port is hard-powered)"
        default 46 if LS_BOARD_P4_NANO
        default 46 if LS_BOARD_P4_WIFI6
        default -1 if LS_BOARD_P4_TOUCH_LCD_4B
        default -1 if LS_BOARD_P4_TOUCH_LCD_43
        default -1
        help
            GPIO driving the load switch that feeds VBUS on the USB host port.
            The firmware drops it to force an unresponsive RTL-SDR to
            re-enumerate ('SDR power', and the automatic stall recovery).

            Set to -1 if the host port is powered directly. On a board with no
            switch the power cycle is skipped rather than driving an unrelated
            pin, and the console says so.

            GPIO46 is confirmed on the ESP32-P4-NANO. It is the assumed default
            on the ESP32-P4-WIFI6 as well because the rest of that board's
            peripheral wiring matches the NANO exactly, but it has not been
            confirmed against hardware - note that GPIO46 is also broken out on
            the pin header of both boards, so the header alone does not settle
            it.

    config LS_DEFAULT_VOLUME
        int "Default audio volume (0-100)"
        range 0 100
        default 50
        help
            Volume used when NVS has no saved value yet - i.e. a fresh board, or
            after an NVS erase. Applied before the boot chime plays.

            Once you change the volume at runtime it is saved to NVS after ~1.5 s
            and that saved value wins on every later boot, so this only governs
            first boot.

    config LS_BLE_HEAD
        bool "BLE control head (Flipper / host over BLE)"
        depends on BT_ENABLED && BT_NIMBLE_ENABLED
        default y
        help
            Build the BLE control head: LakeShark scans for a Flipper running
            the LakeShark app and connects out to it, carrying the same
            command set as the UART head.

            Turn this OFF if you only ever use the UART head or the serial
            console. The BLE link and the whole NimBLE stack drop out of the
            build, which is a large flash and RAM saving on a board that will
            never use it.

            The `ble` console commands still exist with this off - they report
            that the build has no radio head rather than disappearing, so a
            missing command never looks like a firmware fault. The UART head
            is unaffected either way: flipper_link.c is the command parser for
            both transports and is always built.

            This depends on BT_ENABLED, so clearing CONFIG_BT_ENABLED turns it
            off on its own. To drop BLE entirely, clear both - see
            boards/nano_headless_nobt.defaults for a worked example.

    config LAKESHARK_HEADLESS
        bool
        default y
        help
            Every board boots into the radio backend and the console; a board
            with a panel draws the character-grid UI on top of it.

    config LS_C6_LINK
        bool "Bring up the ESP32-C6 co-processor at boot"
        default y
        help
            Attempt esp_hosted_connect_to_slave() during startup.

            Requires compatible ESP-Hosted firmware on the ESP32-C6.
            Disable when the co-processor uses a different protocol.

    config LS_SSH
        bool "SSH for the network terminal"
        default y
        help
            'term ssh on' serves the screen over SSH (libssh, about 230 KB).
            Off, telnet and the web screen still work; the T-Display builds
            turn it off to fit their app slot.

    config EXAMPLE_ENABLE_SD_CARD
        bool "Enable SD Card"
        default n
        help
            Enabling this option will initialize the SD card, so the SD card needs to be inserted into the slot. Additionally, if using the Video Player example, an MJPEG format video must be saved on the SD card.
endmenu

config LS_RX_HEAD
    bool "RADIO: one receiver head with decoder plugins (preview)"
    default n
    help
        Register the RADIO screen: FM's receiver as the RX HEAD, its decoders
        as plugins with their own panels, the shared rail, waterfall strip and
        deck. FM keeps its own screen either way.

config LS_EXAMPLE_APP
    bool "Show native framework example app"
    default n
    help
        Build and register the small shared-widget tap counter example.
